.TH VAULT-MV 1 "September 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-mv \- rename a stored file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault mv
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-vault
.IR DIR ]
.I OLD NEW
.br
.B vault rename
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Renames \fIOLD\fR to \fINEW\fR, which may be in another folder. Fails if
\fINEW\fR exists or is not a valid vault path. File contents are not
re-encrypted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Key file. Default: $VAULT_KEY, else ~/.vault/key.
.TP
.BI \-\-vault " DIR"
Vault directory. Default: $VAULT_DIR, else ~/.vault/store.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VAULT_PASSPHRASE
Passphrase, instead of prompting on the terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1),
.BR vault\-rm (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
